From: PupJune2 <PupJune2@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 19:00:00 +0000
Subject: CromIKO customizable home screen

Let the user arrange the widgets of the new tab page. "Edit home
screen", under the widgets, opens a dialog with the CromIKO mascot
where the user:

- drags the widgets to move them (TalkBack: "Move up", "Move down"),
- makes them small or large,
- turns off the ones they don't need,
- puts back the default home screen with Reset, in one tap.

The new tab page changes behind the dialog right away. The widgets:

- Shortcuts: Bookmarks, Downloads and CromIKO DNS; small shows only
  the icons. It no longer hides with the most visited sites.
- Ads and trackers blocked: small is one line with a smaller mascot.
- Continue reading of manga mode: small has smaller covers.
- Most visited sites: shown or hidden with the setting of "Customize
  Chrome", so both stay the same.
- Recent downloads, new: the downloads that run or wait, with their
  progress and speed from the CromIKO download manager ("In queue",
  "Waiting for Wi-Fi..."), then the ones finished this week. A tap
  opens a finished download, or the download manager; small shows one
  download. It hides when there is nothing to show, like Continue
  reading, and never shows Incognito downloads.

The widgets move between the places they take in the layout, so the
search box and the rest of the page stay where they are. The layout
is kept with the settings of the app (CromIKO on Android has one
browsing profile), like "shortcuts,-shield_stats,downloads:small";
widgets of newer versions go where they are by default.

